binance-connector-cpp provides CMake targets:

    find_package(binance-connector-cpp CONFIG REQUIRED COMPONENTS spot)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE binance::spot)  # binance::common comes with it

Every connector is a feature named like its product, with hyphens: for example
binance-connector-cpp[wallet,derivatives-trading-usds-futures] gives the components and targets
wallet and derivatives_trading_usds_futures, and "all" builds every connector. Without features,
only binance::common is built.
